## What to assert

| Metric | Recommended threshold |
|---|---|
| p95 response time | < 500 ms (adjust per SLA) |
| p99 response time | < 1000 ms |
| Error rate | < 1% |
| Throughput | ≥ expected RPS |

## Evidence format

```
Tool:        {{ performance | upper }}
Test type:   Load (50 VU, 5 min)
Environment: staging
p95:         312 ms  ✅ (threshold: 500 ms)
p99:         480 ms  ✅
Error rate:  0.2%    ✅
Throughput:  48 RPS
```

## Common gotchas

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---|---|
| High error rate in load but not smoke | Connection pool exhaustion — check DB/HTTP pool config |
| p95 spikes at ramp-up only | Cold start / JIT — add a warm-up phase |
| Results differ between runs | External dependency (third-party API, shared DB) — isolate or mock |
| CI passes but prod is slow | Test env has more resources than prod — match specs |
